[center][size=5][b]Recharge Priority[/b][/size]
Recharge from your Ion Batteries and Life Support Gel, not your oxygen.[/center]

[b]What it does[/b]
The quick menu spends the first recharge fuel it can find in a technology's fuel list. The vanilla lists start with the raw substance, so a Life Support recharge reaches for Oxygen and a Hazard Protection recharge reaches for Sodium.
This mod rewrites those lists so the crafted consumable comes first: Ion Batteries for hazard protection and the four environmental shields, Life Support Gel for life support and the underwater shield.
Nothing is removed. When the batteries or gel run out, the game falls back to Oxygen, Sodium, Sodium Nitrate, Dioxite and the rest exactly as before.

[b]Recharge order[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Life Support[/b]: Life Support Gel, Oxygen, Dioxite
[*][b]Hazard Protection[/b]: Ion Battery, Sodium, Sodium Nitrate
[*][b]Thermal shield[/b]: Ion Battery, Phosphorus
[*][b]Cold shield[/b]: Ion Battery, Dioxite
[*][b]Radiation shield[/b]: Ion Battery, Uranium
[*][b]Toxic shield[/b]: Ion Battery, Ammonia
[*][b]Underwater shield[/b]: Life Support Gel, Oxygen
[/list]

[b]Install[/b]
Copy the [i]Recharge Priority[/i] folder into [i]GAMEDATA/MODS[/i], or import the zip with Amethyst or Vortex. There are no installer options.

[b]Compatibility[/b]
[list]
[*]Built for Forsaken
[*]Edits the recharge fuel lists in [i]METADATA/REALITY/TABLES/NMS_REALITY_GCTECHNOLOGYTABLE.MBIN[/i] as EXML line replacements, so it works alongside mods that change other lines of that table
[*]Conflicts with any other mod that rewrites these same seven fuel lists
[*][b].lua [/b]included so you can merge with AMUMSS
[/list]

Built natively on Linux with my [url=https://github.com/SavageCore/AMUMSS/tree/feat/linux-support]AMUMSS Linux port[/url].
